# @vipper/iam-connector (apps/server/src/iam/) publishes to a private registry.
# Scoping it here lets `pnpm add @vipper/...` resolve if you have access; it does
# NOT grant access. Auth is a token that must live in your USER-level ~/.npmrc
# or via `pnpm config set "//npm.vipper.network/:_authToken" <value>` — pnpm
# refuses to expand an env var for registry credentials that come from a
# project .npmrc (this file is committed, and expansion here would let a
# checkout leak whatever the reader's shell happens to export). See
# apps/server/src/iam/iam.client.ts for the fallback this repo actually runs on.
@vipper:registry=https://npm.vipper.network/
